# iceland-device: packages that are installed on the OnePlus Pad 4 but must not be replaced by Fedora's updates.
# A dnf5 repository override (read from /usr/share/dnf5/repos.override.d): it only adds to the three Fedora
# repositories, so the same packages can still come from our local repository (iceland-local) after a new version
# has passed a RAM rehearsal.
#
# 0.28-4 (owner, 12-13 Oct 2026): the MINIMAL hold, the same set the golden's B run refreshes with. Fedora's own kernels
# are refused from every repository by /usr/share/dnf5/libdnf.conf.d/80-iceland-kernel.conf (main excludepkgs). GRUB,
# shim, linux-firmware / qcom-firmware and libcamera now come from Fedora as normal updates:
#   - GRUB / shim stay protected from removal (protected_packages in 80-iceland-kernel.conf);
#   - the tablet's own firmware lies in /usr/lib/firmware/updates (iceland-firmware), which the kernel searches first
#     and which no Fedora firmware package ships: a Fedora firmware update cannot replace it (a path clash would fail
#     the transaction, never overwrite);
#   - libcamera: B145 already runs Fedora's stock libcamera (0.7.1); 0.7.1-2 passed r152 as a normal update.
#
# Held:
# - iio-sensor-proxy, hexagonrpc, libssc: our builds with the sensor-hub support (packaging/sensors); Fedora's
#   iio-sensor-proxy has none, an update to it would end auto-rotate.
# - alsa-ucm (0.24, KEPT in 0.28-4 for a concrete reason): the ALSA UCM data (Fedora's alsa-lib.spec, sub-package
#   alsa-ucm = alsa-ucm-conf). Our sound profile (/usr/share/alsa/ucm2/Qualcomm/kaanapali/OnePlus-Pad4/ +
#   conf.d/kaanapali/oneplus-OnePlusPad4.conf) includes three of its shared files - lib/card-init.conf,
#   lib/ctl-remap.conf, codecs/wcd939x/init.conf (the WCD9395 microphone codec's init) - so a Fedora alsa-ucm update can
#   change the tablet's audio (speaker protection, microphone levels) without a rehearsal; and an alsa-ucm that one day
#   ships the same Qualcomm/kaanapali paths would clash with this package's files. Held, our UCM and the files it
#   includes change only through iceland-device (or a rehearsed alsa-ucm in the local repository). The exact name on
#   purpose: alsa-ucm-utils (alsa-utils.spec: the alsaucm tool) is not UCM data. alsa-ucm requires only alsa-lib >= its
#   own version, so alsa-lib keeps updating.
# - kernel-iceland*, iceland-* (0.28-3, from rehearsal r142): our own packages (the kernel, iceland-device,
#   iceland-firmware). Fedora ships none of these names; should a Fedora repository ever carry one, dnf would compare
#   versions over all enabled repositories, and iceland-local's priority 10 wins only while that repository carries the
#   name (an installed system whose iceland-local was never synced has none). Excluded here, our packages come only
#   from iceland-local.
# An upgrade that cannot be resolved because of a hold is skipped, the rest goes ahead (best=False, skip_broken=True
# in 80-iceland-kernel.conf); iceland-update-check lists what waits.

[fedora]
excludepkgs=iio-sensor-proxy*,hexagonrpc*,libssc*,alsa-ucm,kernel-iceland*,iceland-*

[updates]
excludepkgs=iio-sensor-proxy*,hexagonrpc*,libssc*,alsa-ucm,kernel-iceland*,iceland-*

[updates-testing]
excludepkgs=iio-sensor-proxy*,hexagonrpc*,libssc*,alsa-ucm,kernel-iceland*,iceland-*
